   "claims": [
    "The variance of a binomial distribution is given as: σ² = np(1-p).",
    "The variance of this binomial distribution is equal to np(1-p) = 20 × 0.5 × (1-0.5) = 5.",
    "Take the square root of the variance, and you get the standard deviation of the binomial distribution, 2.24.",
    "If there's a chance of getting a result between the two, such as 0.5, the binomial distribution formula should not be used.",
    "To find the standard deviation of a binomial distribution B(n,p): Compute the variance as n × p × (1-p), where n is the number of trials and p is the probability of successes.",
    "To find this probability, you need to: Recall the binomial distribution formula P(X = r) = nCr × pʳ × (1-p)ⁿ⁻ʳ."
   ],
